    [Doc][Feature] Document enable_force_eplb and warn against production use (#19185)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Makes the `enable_force_eplb` `additional_config` option explicit and
    safe to use:
    
    - Docs: add an `enable_force_eplb` row to the additional_config
    reference table,
    and add a "Performance Ceiling Analysis (`enable_force_eplb`)" section
    to the
      EPLB feature guide with a cross-reference to the reference page.
    - Code: emit a startup warning in `AscendConfig.derive_and_validate`
    whenever
      `enable_force_eplb` is enabled.
    - Test: add a unit test asserting the warning is logged.
    
    `enable_force_eplb` forces a deterministic round-robin expert routing
    that
    replaces the real MoE router output, so it is intended only to measure
    the EPLB
    performance ceiling (upper bound) under an ideally balanced load. The
    warning and
    the docs stress that the model results and accuracy are invalid, it must
    not be
    used in production, and it cannot be combined with
    `eplb_config.dynamic_eplb`.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Yes. `enable_force_eplb` now logs a warning at startup. No change to
    computation
    behavior.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    Documentation and a startup-warning log; no compute path is modified.
    
    - Unit test:
    `tests/ut/test_ascend_config.py::TestAscendConfig::test_enable_force_eplb_logs_production_warning`
      asserts the production warning is emitted when the switch is enabled.
    - The descriptions were verified against the implementation
    (`vllm_ascend/ops/fused_moe/force_eplb.py`,
    `vllm_ascend/ops/fused_moe/routed_experts.py`,
    `vllm_ascend/worker/model_runner_v1.py`, and the mutex check in
    `vllm_ascend/ascend_config.py`).
    - NPU execution of the unit test was not run from this authoring
    environment;
      the change is a log/warning path with no computation impact.
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/c4df37dfcc7f72ca41cd43801a468526ecf99a2b
    
    ---------
    
    Signed-off-by: trae-solo-agent <solo-agent@trae.ai>

